oliver: opened a small PR to update SDK snippets after the stream API rename (start -> open). goal: show migration patterns, safe close, kv cache hint, and a one-line resume note. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/5043 :point_up:

neha: nice. can we add a short migration table (old -> new) and a tiny example per language? keeps signal for customers.

pete: done. i standardized on camelCase for ts/go and snake_case for python. added a contextmanager python pattern and explicit resume_from(token) call.

oliver: python snippet added (context manager form):

```python
# python: recommended pattern after rename
with client.stream.open("gpt-4o-mini", batch_size=4, kv_cache_hint="session:42") as s:
    s.send("extract points:\n" + doc)
    for chunk in s:
        handle(chunk)
# on retry: call s.resume_from(resume_token) with same kv_cache_hint
```

neha: LGTM. one quick extra: add a one-liner under "Retries & resumption": "When resuming, pass the last resume_token and reuse the same kv_cache_hint to avoid duplicated context."

pete: added TS and Go sketches and a short sentence about batch-size tradeoffs (4 low-latency, 8-16 throughput):

```ts
// ts: ensure close to free sockets
const s = await client.stream.open('gpt-4o-mini', { batchSize: 4, kvCacheHint: 'session:42' })
try {
  await s.send('extract points:\n' + doc)
  for await (const chunk of s) {
    onChunk(chunk)
  }
} finally {
  await s.close()
}
```

```go
// go: sketch with resume and jittered backoff
s, err := client.Stream.Open("gpt-4o-mini", StreamOptions{BatchSize:4, KVCacheHint:"session:42"})
if err != nil { log.Fatal(err) }
defer s.Close()
for {
  chunk, err := s.Recv()
  if err != nil { // handle transient, then s.ResumeFrom(token)
    sleep(jitteredBackoff())
    s.ResumeFrom(lastToken)
    continue
  }
  process(chunk)
}
```

